ke  the necessary changes by the end of the  18th of October and I asked them if the  people who will buy the trips and  services before Christmas can already  enjoy better contract and they said yes  however majority of the contracts are  concluded after January so this gave me  a chance also to see a little bit of the  behavior of the consumers anyway the  changes should be fully functional by  the end of this year I also had a  constructive meeting with Facebook and  as you know the Cambridge analytical  which is connected case which is  connected to his facebook services was a  stark reminder that not many people have  clarity on how Facebook uses personal  data of its users and how it works with  third parties like apps games or quiz  creators not many people know that  Facebook has made available their data  to third parties or that for instance it  holds full copyright about any picture  or content you put on it even after you  delete your account and as you may know  I don't have an account but I spoke to  many people that have and many of those  were new things for them and they were  very surprised so we want Facebook to be  absolutely clear to its users about how  the service operates and makes money  Facebook has almost 380 million users in  Europe and I expect Facebook to take  more responsibility for them and I have  no illusion I'm not naive to imagine  that all the people will read the  contracts but I expect many of them to  do so and I expect also Facebook to be  honest with those that go and try to  understand all the consequences of using  their services again on the timing  I appreciate Facebook willingness to  work with us and consume authorities to  solve all their issues also by December  this year so by the 18th of October they  should make the changes so that they can  continue the double check with the CPC  authorities whether this is what we  wanted and by December it should be done  I will not reveal that all right that I  am becoming rather impatient because we  have been in dialogue with Facebook  almost two years and I really want to  see not a progress it's not enough for  me I want to see the results and I want  to see the results which will be  projected in the conditions for the  European consumers let me finalise that  I have a very big respect for work of  the national consumer or thirties this  case which I have been describing to you  is led by the French consumer authority  which is reading this action we are on  the same page  with our colleagues from CPC and from  the French authority  and we see that this is a very useful  attract which needs stronger  coordinating powers which we already  gave them by the new legislation but we  also needed to have unified sanctions  and this is it has been proposed in the  new deal for consumers which the  Commission adopted in April and which is  the package which should improve the  enforcement of consumers rights in a  very big scope and I do hope that the  European Parliament and the member  states will adopt the legislation or the  opposition quickly so that we have this  done as soon as possible in spring next  year thank you very much thank you very  much commissioner I'm sure you found our  press material which we have already  circulated and put online we'll take a  few questions now I have to say  unfortunately only if you will focus on  first on the topic we just discussed  because the Commissioner will have to  catch a plane very soon and run to the  airport so let's start with you Jennifer  can you maybe speak through to Mike the  Guardian thank you on there on Facebook  what what steps would the Commission  take around October if Facebook has  still not complied in a way that you  deemed satisfactory what sanctions might  Facebook face either from the Commission  or from the national authorities  Facebook and face the sanctions from the  national authorities which work under  the CPC network and they will look into  the possible sanctioning after the new  year in case they do not see the  sufficient or no progress or in other  words in case they don't see the things  agreed done in practice so at this  moment the national authorities can  apply the sanctions which are now in in  the legislation and the sanctions differ  from state to state but they will apply  them and after the coordinated action  it's not a photo commission to add the  sanction well in fact this was the part  of our conclusions from my meeting two  days ago that if we do not see the  progress those sanctions will have to  come this is quite clear everything also  to Facebook because I I was quite clear  that we cannot negotiate forever I need  to see the result I just want to ask  about our B&amp;B they are supposed to start  implementing changes on in October right  by the end of the year by the end yes  yes I asked them to give it as a  Christmas present for people before  Christmas okay but they are supposed to  start in October they are supposed to  make all the changes okay there are  still things to be done we discussed the  complexity of announcing the final price  because some of the parts of the price  are changing targets  but they know what we want we know what  they can do and we expect them to do it  by October  so after between October and the end of  the year there might be some some more  clarification but not much the main  thing is to to happen now before the end  of our 18th of October thank you yes so  just a quick question about yesterday  College Commissioner because sorry  listen America fight - what France Lee  Mirman said about situation which is not  improving by service are deteriorating  in Poland and we were discussing the  situation regarding the article 7 and  guck debate where we had reprise of the  Polish authorities and we were speaking  about the possible way forward but no  decision was made yesterday thank you so  please ask - first exam Sultan for all  your active here I'll just like to know  why exactly you don't have a Facebook  account is this because of your own  concerns about data protection or any  other political means why did I cancer  my account don't you have a Facebook  account yeah I had for a short time  Facebook account and it was the channel  of dirt it was I didn't expect such an  influx of of hatred and and I decided to  cancel the account because I realized  that there will be less hatred in Europe  after I do this but I don't want to  avoid the communication with the people  even with the critical people I have for  mail of critical comments and I reply to  those who  do not use vulgar language and so on  this is my nature I speak to everybody  who once normal honest and decent  communication okay thank you very much  are there any further questions yes  regarding the team and that's the danske  bank do you have any comment on the  situation on dance companies thank you  yes I well I will speak about it with  Danish and Finnish an Estonian Minister  of Finance on the 2nd of October because  I want to understand better where the  main errors happened but it was purely  the fault of the lack of due diligence  done by the bank itself or whether there  was also some some mistake as at the  level of the Supervisory Authority of  course this is the case which attracts a  lot of attention from my side because I  am responsible for fighting against  money laundering and this is absolutely  biggest scandal which we have now in  Europe and which is also a very very  unpleasant lesson we are now taking and  which shows the need to be much more  vigilant and much more prudent on  checking the transactions coming to  Europe from from outside after the  discussion with the ministers I will  also discuss with the representation of  the European Banking Authority because  in case we see that this is the mistake  at the level of supervision we will have  to act also on that line and it would  not be the first time I would ask the  EBA too to check